Comment:
 wash ships as a single statically-linked multi-call Go binary. It statically
 links its Go module dependencies and embeds front-end assets (compiled
 web-component bundles, fonts, and player skins) into the binary. Those bundled
 components retain their own upstream licenses; this file covers wash's own
 source. A full per-dependency accounting (Files: stanzas for each vendored Go
 module and embedded asset) would be required before any upload to the Debian
 archive proper.

